\begin{abstract}
We present an automated, \emph{matter-first} search for warp-precursor spacetimes that are genuine solutions to the Einstein equations. MAP-Elites (quality-diversity) and CMA-ES propose sub-luminal scalar shell configurations; \texttt{GRTresna} solves the constraint equations; \texttt{GRTeclyn} evolves the spacetimes in full $3{+}1$ numerical relativity on GPUs; and a \emph{4D evolving null-geodesic tracer} falsifies candidates at high resolution. Our primary result, candidate \texttt{eval\,144}, is a dynamic five-lump exotic shell whose end-to-end 4D shortcut is $f_{\rm geo}=7.96\%$ ($5/5$ rays, Hamiltonian quality OK) at HQ validation ($N=256$, $t=30$), matching the search-tier measurement to $\sim\!0.1\%$. Frozen mid-run geodesics peak higher ($11.5\%$) but collapse by $t=30$; the 4D trace is the authoritative transport certificate. No matter moves superluminally; this is a transient, exotic-matter-supported warp \emph{precursor}, not a transport drive.
\end{abstract}

