\section{Diagnostics and Probe Validation}
\label{sec:probes}

\subsection{Operational and gauge-invariant FTL}

Coordinate operational shortcut $F_{\rm op}$ detects tilted light cones but is partly gauge dependent. The authoritative probe integrates null geodesics,
\begin{equation}
\dot x^\mu=g^{\mu\nu}k_\nu, \qquad \dot k_\mu=-\tfrac12(\partial_\mu g^{\alpha\beta}) k_\alpha k_\beta,
\label{eq:geodesic_eqs}
\end{equation}
on the \emph{evolving} $3{+}1$ metric. Define
\begin{equation}
F_{\rm op}=\frac{t_B^{\rm flat}-t_B^{\rm curved}}{t_B^{\rm flat}},
\label{eq:f_op}
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
f_{\rm geo}=\max\!\left(0,\;\frac{t_{\rm flat}-t_{\rm min}}{t_{\rm flat}}\right),
\label{eq:f_geo}
\end{equation}
with Hamiltonian null-constraint gating ($h_{\rm rel}<10^{-2}$). In HQ mode, five rays are traced from $t_{\rm emit}=0$ through the full cached metric stack ($\sim\!124$ slices).

\subsection{Probe controls}

Prescribed Alcubierre ($f_{\rm geo}\approx32\%$) and Minkowski ($f_{\rm geo}=0$) calibrate the codebase. Candidate \texttt{eval\,086} is the negative control: frozen peak $\sim\!5.8\%$ but 4D HQ trace $\rightarrow0$ ($0/5$ rays, quality fail). \texttt{eval\,144} is the positive control: 4D gain survives HQ.

\section{Results: Verified 4D Warp Precursor (\texttt{eval\,144})}
\label{sec:results}

\subsection{Provenance and genome}

\texttt{eval\,144} is the CMA-ES winner (Stage~2), warm-started from QD \texttt{eval\,156}. The genome is a \emph{dynamic} five-lump exotic shell ($\sim\!91\%$ exotic fraction): Fibonacci sphere layout, momentum-carrying currents, shift-driven motor (\texttt{shell\_static}$\approx0$). HQ replay uses a fresh \texttt{GRTresna} solve at $N=256$, three refinement levels, $t=30$, $126$ frames.

\subsection{4D falsification certificate}

The HQ evolving-geodesic artifact reports:
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
4D $f_{\rm geo}$ & $7.96\%$ \\
rays reached & $5/5$ \\
$t_{\rm emit}$ / $t_{\rm arrival}$ / $t_{\rm flat}$ & $0.00$ / $13.25$ / $14.40$ \\
$h_{\rm quality\_ok}$ & true ($h_{\rm rel}\approx8\times10^{-4}$) \\
search-tier 4D $f_{\rm geo}$ (CMA-ES) & $7.97\%$ ($3/3$ rays) \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The search and HQ measurements agree to $\sim\!0.1\%$ relative---the 4D objective was not a resolution artefact. Effective asymptotic signal speed $\approx c/(1-f_{\rm geo})\approx1.09\,c$ between fixed endpoints; locally all rays remain on the light cone.

